resource "aws_s3_bucket" "exports" {
  bucket_prefix = "exports-"
}

resource "aws_sqs_queue" "export_done" {
  name_prefix = "export-done-"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "exporter" {
  name_prefix = "exporter-"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect    = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com" }
      Action    = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}

# Quick fix from the incident on-call: "just make it work".
resource "aws_iam_policy" "exporter" {
  name_prefix = "exporter-"
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect   = "Allow"
      Action   = "*"
      Resource = "*"
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "exporter" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.exporter.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.exporter.arn
}

content.thinking:
Now I can see the current configuration. The `exporter` policy (lines 22-32) has:
- `Action = "*"` (all actions)
- `Resource = "*"` (all resources)

I need to restrict this to:
1. S3 actions: `s3:GetObject` and `s3:PutObject` on the `exports` bucket (objects within it)
2. SQS action: `sqs:SendMessage` on the `export_done` queue

The bucket is referenced as `aws_s3_bucket.exports` and the queue as `aws_sqs_queue.export_done`.

For the S3 bucket objects, the resource should be `arn:aws:s3:::<bucket-name>/*` 
For the SQS queue, the resource should be the queue ARN.

Let me write the proper least-privilege policy:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "${aws_s3_bucket.exports.arn}/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sqs:SendMessage",
      "Resource": "${aws_sqs_queue.export_done.arn}"
    }
  ]
}
```

Actually, I need to use Terraform string interpolation syntax. The jsonencode function will handle the JSON part, but I need to reference the resources properly:

```hcl
policy = jsonencode({
  Version = "2012-10-17"
  Statement = [
    {
      Effect = "Allow"
      Action = [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ]
      Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.exports.arn}/*"
    },
    {
      Effect = "Allow"
      Action = "sqs:SendMessage"
      Resource = aws_sqs_queue.export_done.arn
    }
  ]
})
```

This gives the exporter role exactly what it needs — read/write on export objects, send permission on the completion queue, nothing else. Time to apply this change to the policy block.

